  This test validates that the method correctly chains the processing steps in the streaming path. It ensures that raw responses go through the processing logic before filtering, which is important for proper response transformation and accumulation of text chunks.

Scenario 30: Generate Content with Non-Streaming and Single Response Emission

Details:
  TestName: generateContentNonStreamingEmitsSingleResponse
  Description: This test verifies that the non-streaming path emits exactly one LlmResponse and then completes, ensuring proper Flowable behavior for single-item streams.
Execution:
  Arrange: Create a mock Client with a mock async.models.generateContent method that returns a CompletableFuture<GenerateContentResponse>. Mock GeminiUtil.prepareGenenerateContentRequest to return a prepared LlmRequest. Create an LlmRequest with valid contents. Set up the CompletableFuture to complete with a valid GenerateContentResponse.
  Act: Invoke generateContent(llmRequest, false) on the Gemini instance and subscribe with a test observer.
  Assert: Verify that exactly one LlmResponse is emitted. Verify that the Flowable completes after emitting the single response. Verify that no additional items are emitted.
Validation:
  This test validates that the non-streaming path correctly implements single-item Flowable semantics. It ensures that the stream completes properly after emitting the response, which is important for proper resource cleanup and preventing hanging subscriptions in reactive applications.

